## Task 1 - Confirm required permissions

Confirm you have the following {{ 'four' if mode == 'uc_table' else 'five' }} permissions. If you don't, request them from your workspace admin.

| Permission | Used in | How to confirm |
|---|---|---|
| Create catalog | Prerequisites Task 3 | [1.1) Catalog creation permission](#11-catalog) |
| SQL Warehouse usage | Steps 2–5 | [1.2) SQL Warehouse usage permission](#12-sql-warehouse) |
| Governed Tag creation | Step 3 (Create Domain) | [1.3) Governed Tag creation permission](#13-governed-tag) |
| Domain creation | Step 3 (Create Domain) | [1.4) Domain creation permission](#14-domain) |
{% if mode != 'uc_table' %}
| {{ source_access_permission }} | Step 1 (Bronze) | [1.5) Source data access](#15-source-access) |
{% endif %}

### 1.1) Catalog creation permission { #11-catalog }

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-01-catalog-menu.png', 'Catalog menu') }}

2. Click the **+** button at the top of the **Catalog** page. If **Create a catalog** appears, you can create catalogs.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-02-create-catalog-menu.png', 'Create a catalog menu') }}

### 1.2) SQL Warehouse usage permission { #12-sql-warehouse }

1. Click **SQL Warehouses** in the left sidebar. Verify that an available SQL Warehouse (e.g., **Serverless Starter Warehouse**) appears in the list.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-03-warehouse-list.png', 'SQL Warehouses list') }}

2. Click the SQL Warehouse you want to use, then click **Permissions** in the top-right corner. Confirm that you or your group has **Can use** or higher permission.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-04-warehouse-permissions.png', 'SQL Warehouse Permissions') }}
{% if engine == 'dbt' %}

!!! warning "Use a serverless SQL warehouse"
    In Step 1, dbt creates Streaming Tables for the Bronze layer, which needs a **Serverless** SQL warehouse. Pick a warehouse whose type is **Serverless** (the **Serverless Starter Warehouse** is).
{% endif %}

### 1.3) Governed Tag creation permission { #13-governed-tag }

When you create a Domain in Step 3, a Governed Tag with the same name is created automatically. You need permission to create Governed Tags.

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar, then click the **Govern** button (shield icon) at the top and select **Governed Tags**.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-05-govern-menu.png', 'Govern > Governed Tags menu') }}

2. Click the **Account Permissions** tab. Confirm that you or your group has **CREATE** permission.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-06-governed-tags-permissions.png', 'Governed Tags > Account Permissions') }}

!!! info "Workspace admins have default permissions"
    Workspace admins have Governed Tag creation permission by default.

### 1.4) Domain creation permission { #14-domain }

1. Click **Discover** in the left sidebar, then click **Create** in the top-right corner. If **Create domain** appears, you can create domains.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-07-create-domain-button.png', 'Discover > Create domain button') }}

!!! info "Permission required to create a domain"
    To create a Domain, you need `MANAGE DISCOVERY` permission. Account admins and workspace admins have this permission by default.
{% if mode != 'uc_table' %}

### 1.5) Source data access { #15-source-access }

{% if mode == 'files' %}
The Bronze tables read raw files from `{{ s.architecture.files.root }}`. You need **{{ source_access_permission }}** on {{ 'the Volume' if s.architecture.files.root.startswith('/Volumes/') else 'the external location that covers this path' }}.

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar and open {{ 'the Volume' if s.architecture.files.root.startswith('/Volumes/') else '**External Data** → **External Locations** and open the location that covers the path' }}.
2. Click **Permissions** and confirm that you or your group has **{{ source_access_permission }}**.
{% elif mode == 'federation' %}
The Bronze tables read from the foreign catalog `{{ s.architecture.federation.foreign_catalog }}`, which mirrors {{ s.architecture.federation.system }} through Lakehouse Federation. You need **{{ source_access_permission }}** on it.

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar and open the foreign catalog `{{ s.architecture.federation.foreign_catalog }}`.
2. Click **Permissions** and confirm that you or your group has **USE CATALOG**, **USE SCHEMA**, and **SELECT**.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

