## Task 3 - Create a catalog

Create a catalog that will be used throughout the lab. All pipeline tables, Metric Views, and Volumes will be created in the `default` schema of this catalog.

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar, then click the **+** button at the top and select **Create a catalog**.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-02-create-catalog-menu.png', 'Create a catalog menu') }}

2. Enter `{{ cat }}` in **Catalog name**. For example, if your name is {{ s.naming.example_user | capitalize }}, enter `{{ ex_cat }}`. Select **Standard** for **Type**, keep **Storage location** at its default, and click **Create**.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-13-create-catalog-dialog.png', 'Create a new catalog dialog') }}

    !!! tip "Naming rule"
        Use only lowercase English letters, numbers, and underscores (`_`) in `<your_name>`. The SQL queries and screenshots in this guide use `{{ s.naming.example_user }}` as an example, so replace it with your name when you follow along.

3. When the **Catalog created!** message appears, click **View catalog**.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-14-catalog-created.png', 'Catalog created message') }}

4. Verify that the `default` schema is automatically created under the catalog. This lab uses the `default` schema; you do not need to create a separate one.

    {{ shot('00-introduction/prereq-15-catalog-default-schema.png', 'Catalog and default schema') }}

